<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI38-QA2-STALE-GATEWAY-SHIM-HARNESS>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI38-QA2-STALE-GATEWAY-SHIM-HARNESS" ;
  triage:title "Stale hermes_gateway_shim scaffolding + false comment in .just/run_hermes_graft_bridge_tests.py, not wired into any CI gate" ;
  triage:description "req-qa's AI38-QA-2 re-verification of feature/pAI-s38-hermes-steer-nudge-delivery @ fd04dcbf found: (1) crates/atm-graft-python/tests/hermes_gateway_shim/gateway/platforms/base.py is dead scaffolding modeling the retired BasePlatformAdapter/MessageEvent/internal=False pattern that AI.38's adapter is explicitly forbidden from using; the current Protocol-based atm_graft_hermes_adapter.py, test_hermes_adapter.py, and test_hermes_bridge.py never import it. (2) .just/run_hermes_graft_bridge_tests.py (invoked by `just test-hermes-graft-bridge`, listed in AI.38's Required Validation) still unconditionally wires HERMES_SRC/gateway_source onto PYTHONPATH pointing at this shim, and retains a comment claiming 'the adapter contract test imports Hermes' gateway modules' -- false for the current tests. This contradicts docs/plans/phase-ai/hermes-graft-adapter-contract.md, which AI.38 corrected to state tests use only checked-in fake steer ports and HermesSteerFixture, with no gateway-shim import. Related: ruthless-boundary-qa's AI38-HERMES-ADAPTER-LINT-GUARD-001 separately found that no CI workflow actually invokes `just test-hermes-graft-bridge`, `test-graft-python`, or `test-hermes-graft-smoke`, and .just/run_pytests.py's build_suite() never discovers crates/*/tests/test_*.py, so the source-scan regression guard in test_hermes_adapter.py (test_adapter_source_forbids_retired_normal_ingress_symbols) never runs in any automated gate." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "implementation-drift" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
